<title>UK: TABLE - Reed Elsevier profits up.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Reed Elsevier profits up.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996 (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Pretax profit				 805   vs 723</p>
<p> Turnover (continuing operations)	3,381 vs 3,205</p>
<p> Turnover (total operations)	     3,381 vs 3,649</p>
<p>NOTE -- Analysts had expected profits mostly in a range between 808.0 million stg and 821.4 million.</p>
<p>Reed Elsevier breaks down its earnings per share and dividend figures between its two parent companies.</p>
<p>For Reed International Plc, the UK arm:</p>
<p> Shr (pence)				    52.6 vs 51.7</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)			     27.2 vs 24.5</p>
<p>For Elsevier, the Dutch arm:</p>
<p> Shr (guilders)				 1.13 vs 1.00</p>
<p> Dividend (gross)(guilders)		 0.76 vs 0.59</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
